 "sections": [
  {
   "id": "in-plain-english",
   "heading": "In plain English",
   "role": "intuition",
   "steps": [
    {
     "id": "in-plain-english-1",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "t": "prose",
       "md": "A geometric series adds up terms that each shrink by the same factor — one, a half, a quarter, and so on. As long as the factor is below one in size, the infinite total is finite and has a simple formula. That one formula prices anything paid over time with discounting, from a perpetuity to a career-long wage premium, and also tells you how shocks persist in a time series."
      },
      {
       "t": "callout",
       "kind": "why",
       "title": "Why it matters",
       "md": "It is the maths behind present values, multipliers and the stability of dynamic systems.",
       "folded": false
      }
     ],
     "words": 87,
     "symbols": []
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "definition",
   "heading": "Definition",
   "role": "definition",
   "steps": [
    {
     "id": "definition-1",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "t": "math",
       "tex": "\\sum_{t=0}^{\\infty}r^t = \\frac{1}{1-r}\\quad(|r|<1), \\qquad \\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}r^t = \\frac{1-r^T}{1-r}"
      },
      {
       "t": "prose",
       "md": "**Proof of the finite sum**: let $S = 1 + r + \\dots + r^{T-1}$. Then $S - rS = 1 - r^T$."
      }
     ],
     "words": 7,
     "symbols": [
      "$r$",
      "$T$",
      "$S$",
      "$t$"
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "present-value",
   "heading": "Present value",
   "role": "depth",
   "steps": [
    {
     "id": "present-value-1",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "t": "prose",
       "md": "Discount factor $\\beta = 1/(1+i)$."
      },
      {
       "t": "table",
       "md": "| Stream | Present value | Example ($c = \\$100$, $i = 5\\%$) |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Perpetuity, first payment in one year | $c/i$ | \\$2,000 |\n| Annuity, $T$ payments | $\\dfrac{c}{i}\\big(1 - (1+i)^{-T}\\big)$ | 30 years: \\$1,537.25 |\n| Growing perpetuity, growth $g < i$ | $c/(i - g)$ | |"
      }
     ],
     "words": 27,
     "symbols": [
      "$T$",
      "$\\beta = 1/(1+i)$",
      "$i$",
      "$c$",
      "$g$"
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "ar-1-processes",
   "heading": "AR(1) processes",
   "role": "depth",
   "steps": [
    {
     "id": "ar-1-processes-1",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "t": "prose",
       "md": "$y_t = \\rho y_{t-1} + \\varepsilon_t$ with $|\\rho| < 1$. Substituting back, $y_t = \\sum_{k\\geq0}\\rho^k\\varepsilon_{t-k}$, so"
      },
      {
       "t": "math",
       "tex": "\\mathrm{Var}(y_t) = \\sigma^2\\sum_{k\\geq0}\\rho^{2k} = \\frac{\\sigma^2}{1-\\rho^2}"
      },
      {
       "t": "prose",
       "md": "At $\\rho = 0.9$ the variance is $5.26\\sigma^2$: persistence amplifies shocks."
      }
     ],
     "words": 11,
     "symbols": [
      "$y_t$, $\\varepsilon_t$",
      "$\\rho$",
      "$\\sigma^2$"
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
